      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1369416091,
      "text": "Paullinia yoco, or yoco, is a liana species of Paullinia which naturally occurs in southern Colombia, Ecuador, and Peru. It was traditionally used by indigenous groups to create a stimulating beverage because of its caffeine and theobromine content and was believed to have medicinal properties as well."
    },
